in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @nl
in @property
in @io

# @code/wasm — the WebAssembly altitude grammar.
#
# Per Alex 2026-06-23: "wasm is @code/wasm." Not a separate family-
# root; lives as a glass instance under @code (matches @code/beam,
# @code/llvm, @code/rust pattern). WASM is just another target_grammar
# in @cascade.
#
# The altitude at which mosaic's shift delegates to a wasm toolchain
# (wasm-pack / wasmtime / wasm-tools / wabt). When mirror.spec
# declares `target binary { altitude @code/wasm, emit wasm-pack }`,
# mosaic walks the target, resolves `@code/wasm` here, then resolves
# `wasm-pack` against this altitude's namespace.
#
# === Why WASM as glass under @code ===
#
# WASM is the portable bytecode target: browsers, edge compute,
# wasmtime serverless. Multiple source grammars cascade to wasm:
# Rust (rustc --target wasm32), AssemblyScript, Gleam (~2026 ETA),
# C/C++ via Emscripten, Go via TinyGo. Per @cascade family-root,
# each (source_grammar, @code/wasm) pair is a cascade species
# shard at `shards/cascade/<source>-wasm.mirror`.
#
# First cascade species discharging this altitude:
#   shards/cascade/rust-wasm.mirror (Stage-1 instance, this session)
#
# === Forward-promised consumers ===
#
# - spectral.engineer @ui delivery (the GPU eigenboard rendering crate
#   at /Users/alexwolf/dev/projects/spectral/crates/ui ships to
#   browser via this WASM altitude per the deployment loop Phase C)
# - Loop 2 (post-v1): @spectral/db ships to browser via WASM
#   cascade (cosmos-mirror as first @spectral/db consumer)
# - Future cascade species: gleam-wasm, assemblyscript-wasm
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-95-cascade-as-
#               loss-lens-substrate-decl.md (ce4874b);
#               shards/cascade.mirror (@cascade family-root that this
#               altitude is target_grammar for).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (@code family-root pattern; wasm is just
#                      another instance per Alex's directive).
# Related shards: shards/code/rust.mirror (@code/rust as paired
#                 cascade source); shards/code/beam.mirror (pattern
#                 reference); shards/cascade.mirror (the cascade
#                 family-root that target_grammar this).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code/wasm.mirror`
# declares `@code/wasm` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

# === build-property surface (settle_on consumers) ===
#
# mirror.spec's `settle_on { binary.validates, binary.runs }` block
# resolves these names against this altitude's grammar. Declared
# here as typed lambdas returning @glass.verdict so the spec parser
# can typecheck the settle_on block.
#
# Body discharged by the toolchain invocation (wasm-validate,
# wasmtime exec, browser load). Pure declaration at the altitude;
# realisation at the @io boundary.
validates(target) -> verdict { \ }
runs(target) -> verdict { \ }

out @code/wasm
out validates
out runs
